(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The limited C API's next slices (queue 262; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 262\"; the user's 244-3 (a) and"] [4 1 "// 244-4 (a)): the functions CPython 3.14.10's Modules/_testlimitedcapi (built by ci into the world beside"] [5 1 "// _ctypes_test) and the pythonapi tests reach, as natives over the handles, ported from CPython 3.14.10's"] [6 1 "// Objects/ (capsule.c, sliceobject.c, moduleobject.c, abstract.c, object.c, longobject.c), Python/ (getargs.c,"] [7 1 "// modsupport.c, ceval.c, sysmodule.c, errors.c, pystrcmp.c, getversion.c) and Include/ (the limited API's"] [8 1 "// declarations, the constants). The PSF's license (LICENSE.md)."] [9 1 "//"] [10 1 "// A function the world's C calls and pyi does not provide is a native that raises NotImplementedError \"pyi's C API"] [11 1 "// does not provide NAME\" (capiMissing: the C stack unwound to the Python call that entered C, as a longjmp would),"] [12 1 "// so a module of the world loads whole and each of its functions fails alone, by a message the classes match."] [25 1 "// capiMissing is the panic of a C API function pyi does not provide."] [28 1 "// missingNative is the native of an undefined C API function."] [33 1 "// recoverMissing turns a capiMissing panic into the Python exception *err (the C stack is restored by World.guard)."] [45 1 "// isCAPIName is a name of the C API (its functions' prefixes)."] [50 1 "// bindMissing makes every undefined C API function of the world a missingNative."] [63 1 "// ---- the C API's data: types and exceptions ----"] [65 1 "// capiTypes are the type objects the limited API names as data (Include/*object.h's PyAPI_DATA(PyTypeObject))."] [76 1 "// bindTypes binds the type objects' structs first (queue 269: every handle made after names them, as ob_type and"] [77 1 "// tp_base), then fills each as CPython's PyTypeObject."] [98 1 "// capsuleType is PyCapsule's type (py's)."] [101 1 "// bindData binds the world's C API data: the type objects' structs become the types' handles, each PyExc_NAME"] [102 1 "// pointer the handle of builtins.NAME, _Py_EllipsisObject and _Py_NotImplementedStruct their singletons'."] [126 1 "// ---- helpers ----"] [128 1 "// excOf is the exception object the error indicator holds (nil: none)."] [136 1 "// badInternalCall is PyErr_BadInternalCall's SystemError."] [139 1 "// errInt sets the error indicator and gives the int -1."] [145 1 "// result is a new reference to o, or C's NULL with err set."] [153 1 "// cstrOrNil is a C string argument (nil for NULL)."] [161 1 "// fromUTF8 is PyUnicode_FromString's decoding of a C string."] [170 1 "// keepCString is s as a C string that lives as long as the process (a const char * the C API returns as borrowed"] [171 1 "// from an object CPython would hold: tp_name, ml_name, a version string), made once per distinct string."] [183 1 "// ssize is a Py_ssize_t clamp of an int (PyLong_AsSsize_t's overflow aside)."] [196 1 "// asLong is PyLong_AsLong (Objects/longobject.c): an int, or an object with __index__."] [212 1 "// asUnsignedMask is PyLong_AsUnsignedLongMask: the int's low 64 bits."] [222 1 "// ---- modules (Objects/moduleobject.c, Python/modsupport.c) ----"] [224 1 "// moduleOf is the module (or its dict) a module handle names."] [232 1 "// addFunctions is PyModule_AddFunctions: each PyMethodDef of the table at defs a built-in function of the module,"] [233 1 "// its self the module."] [261 1 "// cMethod is a PyCFunction of the world bound to self (PyCFunction_NewEx's object)."] [269 2 "// a type's method (queue 268): self is the call's first argument (selfFirst, but METH_STATIC's), defining its"] [270 2 "// type (METH_METHOD's defining_class), qual its name in the messages (Type.name)"] [280 1 "// Builtin is the method as pyi's built-in function."] [285 1 "// call is the vectorcall of a PyCFunction (Objects/methodobject.c: cfunction_call and the METH_* trampolines)."] [289 2 "// the messages name the function as _PyObject_FunctionStr does: module.name() (Objects/methodobject.c)"] [311 25 "// METH_METHOD | METH_FASTCALL | METH_KEYWORDS: (self, defining_class, args, nargsf, kwnames)"] [332 24 "// METH_FASTCALL (| METH_KEYWORDS)"] [354 23 "// METH_NOARGS"] [360 23 "// METH_O"] [366 11 "// METH_VARARGS (| METH_KEYWORDS)"] [406 1 "// moduleFromDef is PyModule_Create2's module: m_name, m_doc and m_methods of the PyModuleDef at def."] [413 46 "// md_state (queue 269: PyModule_GetState), zeroed"] [426 1 "// ---- PyArg_Parse, PyArg_ParseTuple (Python/getargs.c) ----"] [428 1 "// vgetargs is vgetargs1_impl: the arguments (one, compat, for PyArg_Parse) converted by format into the pointers."] [519 1 "// seterror is getargs.c's seterror: a conversion's message as \"fname() argument N must be ...\"."] [543 1 "// argState is the va_list of the pointers the units store through."] [557 1 "// converterr is getargs.c's converterr."] [569 1 "// convert is convertsimple's units (b B h H i I n l k L K f d p y y# s s# z z# O O! and the tuple units aside):"] [570 1 "// a message (the conversion's failure) or an error (an exception the conversion raised)."] [697 4 "// getbuffer's PyObject_GetBuffer raised (the message is the buffer protocol's)"] [732 1 "// ---- Py_BuildValue (Python/modsupport.c) ----"] [734 1 "// buildValue is Py_BuildValue's do_mkvalue over the format's units and the variadic arguments."] [852 2 "// the top level: one unit is its value, none is None, several a tuple"] [874 1 "// ---- capsules (Objects/capsule.c) ----"] [876 1 "// cCapsule is a capsule C made: its pointer, name (0: NULL), context and destructor in the world."] [903 1 "// newCapsule is PyCapsule_New: a capsule of py's PyCapsule type, its destructor called on the library's next call"] [904 1 "// after the capsule is collected."] [919 5 "// the destructor gets the capsule (a fresh handle: the capsule is Go's until the call ends)"] [930 1 "// capsuleImport is PyCapsule_Import."] [964 1 "// decodeReplace is PyUnicode_FromFormat's %s: UTF-8 decoded with \"replace\"."] [973 1 "// ---- slices (Objects/sliceobject.c) ----"] [977 1 "// evalSliceIndex is _PyEval_SliceIndex: None leaves *v, an index clamps to Py_ssize_t."] [1003 1 "// sliceUnpack is PySlice_Unpack."] [1038 1 "// sliceAdjust is PySlice_AdjustIndices."] [1082 1 "// sliceGetIndices is PySlice_GetIndices: -1 without an exception for what it refuses."] [1135 1 "// ---- the frames (Python/ceval.c) ----"] [1137 1 "// callerFrame is the Python frame that called C (sys._getframe(0) seen from the native)."] [1158 1 "// frameLocals is PyEval_GetFrameLocals: a function's locals as a dict snapshot (PEP 667), a module's or class's"] [1159 1 "// namespace itself."] [1171 1 "// funcName and funcDesc are PyEval_GetFuncName and PyEval_GetFuncDesc."] [1207 1 "// sysCall calls sys.NAME(args...)."] [1220 1 "// sysGetObject is PySys_GetObject: sys's attribute (nil when absent; a decoding error is unraisable)."] [1239 1 "// ---- the natives ----"] [1241 1 "// version strings (Python/getversion.c, getplatform.c, getcopyright.c, getcompiler.c, Modules/getbuildinfo.c)"] [1257 2 "// version and build"] [1262 2 "// _Py_GetBuiltWithAssert (Python/getversion.c's): pyi's own runtime asserts nothing in C"] [1271 2 "// modules"] [1353 2 "// argument parsing and building"] [1378 2 "// errors (Python/errors.c)"] [1478 2 "// capsules"] [1512 2 "// the evaluation's state"] [1542 2 "// frames (Objects/frameobject.c: PyFrame_GetLocals and the others, new references)"] [1578 2 "// the GIL (Python/pystate.c): pyi's threads hold it when they run Python, so a thread that calls C holds it"] [1579 2 "// already: PyGILState_Ensure gives PyGILState_LOCKED (0) and Release has nothing to give back"] [1583 2 "// sys (Python/sysmodule.c)"] [1623 2 "// slices"] [1695 2 "// strings compared (Python/pystrcmp.c)"] [1728 1 "// cstr8 is a C string argument's bytes (nil for NULL)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[35 19] [36 31] [54 30] [82 27] [83 29] [10